---

# Explainability

CAS should explain recommendations using adaptation principles.

Example

Today's heavy strength session primarily targets neural adaptation.

Because neural adaptations recover relatively quickly,

high-quality repetitions are prioritized over volume.

---

# Scientific Foundation

The model is continuously updated according to the best available scientific evidence.

Scientific uncertainty should always be acknowledged.

The model remains evidence-informed,

not evidence-limited.

---

# Future Expansion

Future versions may integrate

Genomic information.

Blood biomarkers.

Hormonal responses.

Velocity-based adaptation.

AI-based adaptation prediction.

These additions should remain compatible with the existing model.

---

# Success Criteria

The model succeeds when

Training produces predictable adaptations.

Programming remains biologically coherent.

Recovery supports adaptation.

Performance improves sustainably.

Athletes understand why training works.

---

# Final Principle

The goal of training is not exercise.

The goal of training is adaptation.

The better CAS understands adaptation,

the better it can develop combat athletes.